#. §0: `A`
#. §1: `U`
#. §2: `Aᶜ`
#. §3: `A`
#. §4: `Aᶜ`
#. §5: `U`
#. §6: `A`
#. §7: `ᶜ`
#. §8: `\\compl`
#. §9: `\\^c`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L02compdef
msgid "If §0 is a of objects from the universe §1, then §2 is the complement of §3; that is,\n"
"§4 is the set of objects from §5 that are not elements of §6.  You can enter the symbol §7\n"
"by typing §8 or §9."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FamInter.L03interpair
msgid "Intersection of a pair"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `exact`
#. §1: `exact`
#. §2: `h1`
#. §3: `x ∈ A`
#. §4: `x ∈ B`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L02subhyp
msgid "This example is a better illustration of how the §0 tactic is usually\n"
"used.  Often §1 is followed by an expression that combines assumptions\n"
"to prove the goal.  In later levels, we will see other ways in which\n"
"assumptions can be combined to prove a goal.\n"
"\n"
"Note that in this proof, §2 could be thought of as a function that can be\n"
"applied to a proof of any statement of the form §3 to produce a proof\n"
"of §4.  Many proofs in Lean behave like functions."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `∅`
#. §1: `∅ ⊆ A`
#. §2: `Subset.refl`
#. §3: `A`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L01proveexists
msgid "By the way, another set that would have worked as a witness for the existential goal in this\n"
"theorem is the empty set, denoted §0.  However, to justify the use of that witness you would\n"
"have had to prove §1.  Since we already have the theorem §2, it was easier to use\n"
"§3 as the witness.\n"
"\n"
"Now that you know how to prove existential statements, you're ready to start working with\n"
"unions of families."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h}»`
#. §1: `have «{h}»BC : «{x}» ∈ B ∪ C := «{h}».right`
#: Game.Levels.Combo.L03inter_distrib_union
msgid "It may help you see how to proceed if you separate\n"
"out the second half of §0 as a separate assumption.\n"
"You can do this with §1."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Union.L05union_comm
msgid "Union is commutative"
msgstr ""

#: GameServer.RpcHandlers
msgid "intermediate goal solved! 🎉"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `compl_subset_compl_of_subset «{h1}»`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L05compsubiff
msgid "§0 will prove the goal."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Union.L06union_assoc
msgid "Union is associative"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `apply`
#. §1: `t`
#. §2: `t ?`
#. §3: `P`
#. §4: `t`
#. §5: `apply t`
#. §6: `P`
#. §7: `t`
#. §8: `apply t`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L04compcomp
msgid "You can use the §0 tactic to work backwards from the goal.  Suppose you think that you\n"
"will be able to use some theorem §1 to prove the goal.  In other words, you think there\n"
"is a proof of the goal of the form §2, where the question mark needs to be replaced\n"
"with a proof of some statement §3 to which the theorem §4 must be applied.  The tactic\n"
"§5 will then set §6 as your goal.  If §7 must be applied to more than one proof to\n"
"establish the goal, then §8 will set all of the needed proofs as goals."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P x`
#. §1: `x`
#. §2: `∃ x, P x`
#. §3: `x`
#. §4: `P x`
#. §5: `∃`
#. §6: `\\exists`
#. §7: `∃ x, P x`
#. §8: `h : P a`
#. §9: `a`
#. §10: `Exists.intro a h`
#. §11: `∃ x, P x`
#. §12: `exact Exists.intro a h`
#. §13: `P a`
#. §14: `apply Exists.intro a`
#. §15: `P a`
#. §16: `use a`
#. §17: `P a`
#. §18: `P a`
#. §19: `h : ∃ x, P x`
#. §20: `obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := h`
#. §21: `w`
#. §22: `hw : P w`
#. §23: `⟨ ⟩`
#. §24: `\\<`
#. §25: `\\>`
#. §26: `\\langle`
#. §27: `\\rangle`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L01proveexists
msgid "If §0 represents a statement about §1, then §2 means \"there is at least one\n"
"§3 such that §4 is true\".  To enter the symbol §5, type §6.\n"
"\n"
"### If your goal is §7\n"
"\n"
"If you have §8, for some object §9, then §10 is a proof of §11,\n"
"so §12 will close the goal.\n"
"If you think §13 is true, but you don't yet have a proof of it, then §14\n"
"will set §15 as your goal.  The tactic §16 does the same thing, but it also tries to\n"
"prove §17; if it doesn't succeed, then it leaves §18 as a goal for you to prove.\n"
"\n"
"### If you have an assumption §19\n"
"\n"
"The tactic §20 will\n"
"introduce a new object §21 and a new assumption §22 into the proof.  To enter the\n"
"angle brackets §23, type either §24 and §25 or §26 and §27."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P x`
#. §1: `x`
#. §2: `h : P a`
#. §3: `a`
#. §4: `Exists.intro a h`
#. §5: `∃ x, P x`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L01proveexists
msgid "If §0 represents a statement about §1 and you have §2, for some object §3, then\n"
"§4 is a proof of §5."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `¬A ⊆ B`
#. §1: `h3 : A ⊆ B`
#. §2: `by_contra h3`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L01contra
msgid "For the theorem in this level, your goal is §0.  To use proof by contradiction\n"
"in this proof, you must begin by introducing the assumption §1.  To do that, type\n"
"§2"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P x`
#. §1: `x`
#. §2: `∀ x, P x`
#. §3: `x`
#. §4: `P x`
#. §5: `∀`
#. §6: `\\forall`
#. §7: `∀ x, P x`
#. §8: `intro t`
#. §9: `t`
#. §10: `P t`
#. §11: `t`
#. §12: `h : ∀ x, P x`
#. §13: `a`
#. §14: `h a`
#. §15: `P a`
#. §16: `a`
#. §17: `x`
#. §18: `U`
#. §19: `a`
#. §20: `U`
#. §21: `x`
#. §22: `U`
#. §23: `a`
#. §24: `Set U`
#: Game.Levels.FamInter.L01intersub
msgid "If §0 represents a statement about an unspecified object §1, then §2 means\n"
"\"for all §3, §4 is true\".  To enter the symbol §5, type §6.\n"
"\n"
"### If your goal is §7\n"
"\n"
"The tactic §8 will introduce a new object §9 into the proof, and set the goal to be §10.\n"
"Be sure to use a variable §11 that is not already being used to stand for some object.\n"
"\n"
"### If you have an assumption §12\n"
"\n"
"If §13 stands for some object, then §14 is a proof of §15.  Note that §16 must be the\n"
"right *type* of object.  For example, if §17 stands for an object in the universe §18, then\n"
"§19 must have type §20; if §21 stands for a set of objects from the universe §22, then §23 must\n"
"have type §24."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A`
#. §1: `B`
#. §2: `A`
#. §3: `B`
#. §4: `A ∪ B`
#. §5: `A`
#. §6: `B`
#. §7: `A ∪ B`
#. §8: `A`
#. §9: `B`
#. §10: `A`
#. §11: `B`
#. §12: `A ∪ B`
#: Game.Levels.Union
msgid "If §0 and §1 are sets, then the *union* of §2 and §3, denoted\n"
"§4, is the set you get by throwing all the elements of §5 and §6\n"
"together into one set.  In other words, for an object to be an element of\n"
"§7, it must be an element of either §8 or §9, or both.\n"
"\n"
"For example, if §10 is the set of all people under 30, and §11 is the set of\n"
"all people over 20, then §12 is the set of all people.\n"
"\n"
"In this world you'll prove some basic properties of unions of sets."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x ∈ A`
#. §1: `x`
#. §2: `A`
#. §3: `∈`
#. §4: `\\mem`
#. §5: `\\in`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L01exact
msgid "§0 means that §1 is an element of §2.  To enter the symbol §3, type\n"
"§4 or §5."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `apply Iff.intro`
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L08inter_assoc
msgid "Since your goal is an \"if and only if\" statement, a good next step\n"
"is §0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $A \\subseteq B$
#. §1: $B^c \\subseteq A^c$
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L03compsub
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L02elt_inter_elt_right
msgid "Suppose §0.  Then §1."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Subset.L04imp
msgid "Implication"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h1}»`
#. §1: `«{x}» ∈ ⋃₀ F`
#. §2: `apply «{h1}»`
#. §3: `«{x}» ∈ ⋃₀ F`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L06unionsub
msgid "Notice that §0 could be applied to a proof of §1 to\n"
"prove the goal.  That means that §2 will set §3 as the goal."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L04unionpair
msgid "Union of a pair"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A`
#. §1: `Subset.refl`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L01proveexists
msgid "Your goal says that there is a set that is a subset of §0.\n"
"The theorem §1 suggests such a set."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rewrite`
#. §1: `rewrite`
#. §2: `rw`
#. §3: `rewrite`
#. §4: `rw`
#. §5: `rewrite`
#. §6: `compl_subset_compl_of_subset`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L03compsub
msgid "The §0 tactic is often useful for writing out definitions.  For more information about\n"
"how it works, click on §1 in the list of tactics on the right.  You can also use §2\n"
"instead of §3.  (There is actually a small difference between the tactics §4 and\n"
"§5, but the difference won't concern us in this game.)\n"
"\n"
"You'll find the theorem you proved in this level listed as §6 in the list of\n"
"theorems on the right.  This theorem will be useful in the last level of this world."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Combo.L02compint
msgid "Do you see how you can now use the theorem from the previous level?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h4}» : x ∈ B`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L03have
msgid "Notice that §0 has been added to the list of assumptions.\n"
"Can you complete the proof now?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rewrite [mem_setOf]`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L07eltwiseinter
msgid "You can use §0 to write out the meaning of the goal."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FamCombo.L04threefam
msgid "A theorem about three families"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FamCombo.L08singleton
msgid "A set that must be a singleton"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `cases`
#. §1: `rcases`
#. §2: `rcases`
#: Game.Levels.Union.L03cases
msgid "Note that Lean also has a §0 tactic, but the syntax is a little more complicated.\n"
"That's why we have chosen to use the §1 tactic.\n"
"\n"
"The §2 tactic has other uses.  However, in this game we will be using it only with\n"
"assumptions that are \"or\" statements, to break the proof into cases."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `Aᶜᶜ ⊆ A`
#. §1: `A ⊆ Aᶜᶜ`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L04compcomp
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L05subint
msgid "Your immediate goal now is to prove that §0.  Once you close that goal,\n"
"you'll be asked to prove the second goal, §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $A$
#. §1: $B$
#. §2: $A \\subseteq B$
#. §3: $x \\in A$
#. §4: $x \\in B$
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L02subhyp
msgid "Suppose §0 and §1 are sets, §2, and §3.\n"
"Then §4."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A`
#. §1: `B`
#. §2: `A`
#. §3: `B`
#. §4: `A ∩ B`
#. §5: `A ∩ B`
#. §6: `A`
#. §7: `B`
#. §8: `A`
#. §9: `B`
#. §10: `A ∩ B`
#: Game.Levels.Inter
msgid "If §0 and §1 are sets, then the *intersection* of §2 and §3, denoted\n"
"§4, is the set of elements that the two sets have in common.  In other words,\n"
"for an object to be an element of §5, it must be an element of both §6 and §7.\n"
"\n"
"For example, if §8 is the set of all round things, and §9 is the set of all red things,\n"
"then §10 is the set of all round red things.\n"
"\n"
"In this world you'll prove some basic properties of intersections of sets."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{x}» ∈ A ∨ «{x}» ∈ B`
#. §1: `«{x}» ∈ A`
#. §2: `«{x}» ∈ B`
#. §3: `«{x}» ∈ C`
#. §4: `with`
#. §5: `rcases`
#: Game.Levels.Union.L03cases
msgid "Now you have *two* goals.  For the first, the assumption §0 has been\n"
"replaced with §1, and for the second it has been replaced with §2.  In both\n"
"cases, you must prove §3.  The two identifiers after §4 in the §5 tactic\n"
"are used as the identifiers of the new assumptions in the two cases."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `F`
#. §1: `U`
#. §2: `F`
#. §3: `U`
#. §4: `F`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion
msgid "If §0 is a family of sets from §1, then the *union* of §2 is the set of all objects from\n"
"§3 that belong to at least one element of §4.  We'll investigate unions of families in this\n"
"world."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $F$
#. §1: $G$
#. §2: $F \\subseteq G$
#. §3: $\\bigcap G \\subseteq \\bigcap F$
#: Game.Levels.FamInter.L02intersubinter
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L03unionsubunion
msgid "Suppose §0 and §1 are families of sets and §2.\n"
"Then §3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A ∩ B ∪ A ∩ C`
#. §1: `(A ∩ B) ∪ (A ∩ C)`
#: Game.Levels.Combo.L03inter_distrib_union
msgid "Once again, Lean has left out some parentheses that it regards as unnecessary.\n"
"Lean gives intersection higher precedence than union, so it interprets\n"
"§0 as §1."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Union.L06union_assoc
msgid "Do you know which half of the goal you're going to prove now?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x : U`
#. §1: `A : Set U`
#. §2: `B : Set U`
#. §3: `mem_union x A B`
#. §4: `x ∈ A ∪ B ↔ x ∈ A ∨ x ∈ B`
#. §5: `Set.mem_union`
#: Game.Levels.Union.L02subunion
msgid "If you have §0, §1, and §2, then §3 is a proof of the\n"
"statement §4.  In Mathlib, the name of this theorem is §5."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `h1 : A ⊆ B`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L05compsubiff
msgid "Of course, you should begin by introducing the assumption\n"
"§0."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Subset.L02subhyp
msgid "A subset hypothesis"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x ∈ A → x ∈ C`
#. §1: `x ∈ A`
#. §2: `h3`
#. §3: `intro h3`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L04imp
msgid "Since our goal in this level is the statement §0, our first step for\n"
"this proof is to assume §1.  To introduce that assumption,\n"
"assigning it the identifier §2, type §3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `F`
#. §1: `G`
#. §2: `F ⊆ G`
#. §3: `⋂₀ G`
#. §4: `F`
#. §5: `⋂₀ G ⊆ ⋂₀ F`
#: Game.Levels.FamInter.L02intersubinter
msgid "In this level we have two families of sets, §0 and §1, with §2.  That means that\n"
"§3 is the intersection of a family of sets that includes all the sets in §4, plus\n"
"perhaps more sets.  You're going to prove that intersecting this larger collection of sets\n"
"leads to a smaller result; more precisely, you're going to prove that §5.\n"
"\n"
"Of course, by now you know how to start a proof that one set is a subset of another."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `mem_inter_iff`
#. §1: `x : U`
#. §2: `A : Set U`
#. §3: `B : Set U`
#. §4: `mem_inter_iff x A B`
#. §5: `x ∈ A ∩ B ↔ x ∈ A ∧ x ∈ B`
#. §6: `rewrite [mem_inter_iff x A B]`
#. §7: `x ∈ A ∩ B`
#. §8: `x ∈ A ∧ x ∈ B`
#. §9: `x`
#. §10: `A`
#. §11: `B`
#. §12: `rewrite [mem_inter_iff]`
#. §13: `rewrite [mem_inter_iff] at h`
#. §14: `h`
#. §15: `mem_compl_iff`
#. §16: `mem_inter_iff`
#. §17: `rfl`
#. §18: `∩`
#. §19: `\\inter`
#. §20: `\\cap`
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L02elt_inter_elt_right
msgid "In this level, we'll need to use the definition of \"intersection\".  The theorem that\n"
"expresses that definition is called §0.  If you have §1, §2, and\n"
"§3, then §4 is a proof of the statement §5.\n"
"As we saw in Complement World, that means that the tactic §6 can be\n"
"used to replace §7 in the goal with §8.  Usually Lean can figure out\n"
"§9, §10, and §11 on its own, so you can just write §12, and you can\n"
"use §13 to do the replacement in an assumption §14 rather than\n"
"the goal.\n"
"\n"
"Like §15, §16 can be proven by using the §17 tactic.  But we\n"
"won't ask you to prove it; it is pre-defined in this game.  To enter the symbol §18, you\n"
"can type §19 or §20."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Inter.L07inter_comm
msgid "We'll prove one more property of intersections in the next level."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $F$
#. §1: $G$
#. §2: $\\bigcup (F \\cup G) =
#. (\\bigcup F) \\cup (\\bigcup G)$
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L05unionunion
#: Game.Levels.FamCombo.L05unionintcompunion
#: Game.Levels.FamCombo.L07unionintcompint
msgid "Suppose §0 and §1 are families of sets.  Then §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A`
#. §1: `B`
#. §2: `A ∩ B`
#. §3: `A`
#. §4: `B`
#. §5: `∩`
#. §6: `\\inter`
#. §7: `\\cap`
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L02elt_inter_elt_right
msgid "If §0 and §1 are sets, then §2 is the intersection of §3 and §4.\n"
"To enter the symbol §5, type §6 or §7."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `compl_compl`
#. §1: `Aᶜᶜ = A`
#. §2: `Bᶜᶜ = B`
#. §3: `«{h2}»`
#. §4: `rewrite`
#. §5: `P ↔ Q`
#. §6: `P`
#. §7: `Q`
#. §8: `t`
#. §9: `p = q`
#. §10: `rewrite [t]`
#. §11: `p`
#. §12: `q`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L05compsubiff
msgid "Fortunately, we can use the theorem §0 to prove §1 and\n"
"§2, and those statements should get us from §3 to the goal.\n"
"We have seen in previous levels that the §4 tactic can be applied to a proof of a\n"
"statement of the form §5 to replace §6 with §7.  The tactic can also be applied to\n"
"equations: if §8 is a proof of an equation §9, then §10 will\n"
"replace §11 with §12."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{x}» : U`
#. §1: `«{x}» ∈ A ∩ B ∩ C ↔ «{x}» ∈ A ∩ (B ∩ C)`
#. §2: `A ∩ B ∩ C`
#. §3: `A ∩ (B ∩ C)`
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L08inter_assoc
msgid "Notice that Lean has introduced the new object §0 into the proof, and\n"
"your goal is now §1.  Proving this goal will show that\n"
"§2 and §3 have exactly the same elements, and by the principle of\n"
"extensionality, that will show that the sets are equal."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x : U`
#. §1: `A : Set U`
#. §2: `B : Set U`
#. §3: `mem_inter_iff x A B`
#. §4: `x ∈ A ∩ B ↔ x ∈ A ∧ x ∈ B`
#. §5: `Set.mem_inter_iff`
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L02elt_inter_elt_right
msgid "If you have §0, §1, and §2, then §3 is a proof of the\n"
"statement §4.\n"
"In Mathlib, the name of this theorem is §5."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `And.intro «{h}».right «{h}».left`
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L06inter_sub_swap
msgid "Now §0 proves the goal."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Union.L01or
msgid "Now we're ready to start proving theorems about unions."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `h`
#. §1: `x ∈ A`
#. §2: `x ∈ A`
#. §3: `h : P`
#. §4: `P`
#. §5: `h`
#. §6: `P`
#. §7: `exact`
#. §8: `exact`
#. §9: `exact`
#. §10: `h`
#. §11: `x ∈ A`
#. §12: `h`
#. §13: `exact`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L01exact
msgid "Congratulations! You have completed your first verified proof!\n"
"\n"
"Although this theorem was trivial, it illustrates an important fact: although we\n"
"called §0 an *identifier* for the assumption §1, it is also recognized by Lean\n"
"as a *proof* of the statement §2.  Any time you see §3\n"
"listed as an assumption, where §4 is some statement, that means that Lean will\n"
"recognize §5 as a proof of the statement §6.\n"
"\n"
"Remember that §7 is a *tactic*. If you ever want information about the §8 tactic,\n"
"you can click on §9 in the list of tactics on the right.\n"
"\n"
"Note that, although §10 was a proof of the goal §11, you could not have closed the goal by\n"
"simply typing §12 in the text box.  Throughout this game, every move you make must invoke a tactic.\n"
"\n"
"Now click on \"Next\" to see a more interesting use of the §13 tactic."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Inter.L08inter_assoc
msgid "Intersection is associative"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `⋃₀ F`
#. §1: `(⋃₀ G)ᶜ`
#. §2: `F`
#. §3: `G`
#: Game.Levels.FamCombo.L05unionintcompunion
msgid "What happens if you intersect §0 with §1, for two families §2 and §3?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `{a}`
#. §1: `a`
#. §2: `mem_singleton_iff`
#. §3: `mem_singleton_iff`
#. §4: `x ∈ {a} ↔ x = a`
#: Game.Levels.FamCombo.L08singleton
msgid "The notation §0 denotes a set whose only element is §1; such a set is called a *singleton*\n"
"set.  The theorem §2 expresses the definition of singleton sets: §3 is\n"
"a proof of any statement of the form §4."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FamInter.L06eltwiseunion
msgid "You've finished Family Intersection World!  As you might guess, you can also take the union of\n"
"a family of sets.  Can you guess how to define it?  Continue on to Family Union World to see\n"
"if your guess is right."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Combo.L03inter_distrib_union
