#. §1: `use A`
#. §2: `use`
#. §3: `A`
#. §4: `t`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L02subunion
msgid "There is another tactic you could have used to complete this proof.  Instead of\n"
"§0, you could write §1.  The §2 tactic is actually a powerful\n"
"tactic.  Not only does it fill in §3 for §4 in the existential goal, it then tries to\n"
"complete the proof on its own--and in this case, it would have succeeded!"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rewrite [compl_inter]`
#. §1: `rewrite [compl_inter]`
#. §2: `compl_inter`
#. §3: `compl_inter B C`
#. §4: `(B ∩ C)ᶜ = Bᶜ ∪ Cᶜ`
#. §5: `compl_inter Aᶜ (B ∩ C)ᶜ`
#. §6: `(Aᶜ ∩ (B ∩ C)ᶜ)ᶜ = Aᶝᶜ ∪ (B ∩ C)ᶜᶜ`
#. §7: `rewrite [compl_inter]`
#. §8: `compl_inter`
#: Game.Levels.Combo.L04union_distrib_inter
msgid "You might be tempted to use §0 as your next step.  But\n"
"in this situation, §1 is ambiguous, because there are\n"
"two ways that the theorem §2 could be applied to rewrite the goal: §3\n"
"is a proof of §4 and §5 is a proof of\n"
"§6, and either one of those equations could be used to\n"
"rewrite the goal.  If you say §7, then Lean will pick one of those two\n"
"rewriting steps, and it might not pick the one you wanted.  So you'd better say explicitly\n"
"what you want Lean to apply the theorem §8 to."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A ∪ B = B ∪ A`
#. §1: `A ∪ B ⊆ B ∪ A`
#: Game.Levels.Union.L04union_sub_swap
msgid "In the next level we're going to prove that union is commutative; that is,\n"
"§0.  We're going to imitate the approach we used in Intersection World\n"
"to prove that intersection is commutative.  We begin by proving §1."
msgstr ""

