#. §19: `\\rangle`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L03unionsubunion
msgid "In this level we have two families of sets, §0 and §1, with §2.  In Family Intersection\n"
"World, you proved that in this situation, §3.  In this level, you'll prove that\n"
"with family unions, it works the other way: §4.\n"
"\n"
"We'll need a new tactic for this proof.  An assumption of the form §5 tells you that\n"
"an object with a certain property exists.  If you have such an assumption, then it is usually\n"
"helpful to introduce a name for such an object.  You can do this with the §6 tactic.  If\n"
"you write §7, then Lean will introduce a new object §8 and a new assumption\n"
"§9.  Thus, the object §10 is a witness for the existential assumption §11.  Note that\n"
"in the §12 tactic, §13 and §14 must be enclosed in angle brackets: §15.  You can\n"
"enter these by typing either §16 and §17 or §18 and §19."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Subset.L06subtrans
msgid "Subset is transitive"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `Subset.trans`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L06subtrans
msgid "The theorem you have proven in this level shows that the subset relation has\n"
"a property called *transitivity*.  We have given the theorem the name §0."
msgstr ""

