#: Game.Levels.Subset
msgid "Welcome to Subset World! In this world you will learn about sets and\n"
"subsets, and you will also learn the basics of proving theorems in Lean.\n"
"\n"
"The elements of the sets in this world will come from a universe called §0.\n"
"To specify that an\n"
"object §1 belongs to the universe §2, we write §3.  To specify\n"
"that §4 is a set of objects from §5, we write §6.  (The terminology used\n"
"in Lean is that §7 has *type* §8 and §9 has *type* §10.)  To\n"
"say that §11 is an element of §12, we write §13.  (You can enter\n"
"the symbol §14 by typing §15 or §16, followed by a space.)\n"
"\n"
"You will prove theorems in this game by using tools called *tactics*.\n"
"The aim is to prove the theorem by applying tactics\n"
"in the right order.\n"
"\n"
"Let's learn some basic tactics. Click on \"Start\" below\n"
"to get started."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x`
#. §1: `U`
#. §2: `A`
#. §3: `U`
#. §4: `x ∈ A`
#. §5: `x ∈ A`
#. §6: `U : Type`
#. §7: `x : U`
#. §8: `A : Set U`
#. §9: `h : x ∈ A`
#. §10: `h`
#. §11: `x ∈ A`
#. §12: `exact`
#. §13: `exact`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L01exact
msgid "# Read this first\n"
"\n"
"Each level in this game involves proving a mathematical statement (the \"Goal\").\n"
"When you give a proof of this statement that\n"
"is accepted by Lean, we say that you have *closed* the goal.\n"
"\n"
"In this first level you're going to prove that if §0 belongs to the universe §1,\n"
"§2 is a set of objects from §3, and §4, then §5.  You should see\n"
"§6, §7, and §8 under *Objects* in the pane to the right, and\n"
"§9 under *Assumptions*.  The letter §10 here is called an *identifier*\n"
"for the assumption §11.\n"
"\n"
"You will prove goals in Lean using *tactics*.  The first tactic you're\n"
"going to learn is called §12, and it is used to close the goal.\n"
"You can close the goal by typing §13 followed by a proof of the goal."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `Subset.refl A`
#. §1: `A ⊆ A`
#. §2: `have h : A ⊆ A := Subset.refl A`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L01proveexists
msgid "Recall that §0 is a proof of §1.\n"
"So start your proof with §2."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L03unionsubunion
msgid "Union of larger family is larger"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FamInter.L05subinter
msgid "Notice that the parentheses in the next goal are necessary, to indicate that the universal\n"
"quantifier applies only to the subset statement.  Without the parentheses, Lean would interpret\n"
"the universal quantifier as applying to the entire rest of the statement."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `by_contra`
#. §1: `¬`
#. §2: `by_contra`
#. §3: `False`
#. §4: `False`
#. §5: `h1 : P`
#. §6: `h2 : ¬P`
#. §7: `P`
#. §8: `exact h2 h1`
#. §9: `exact h1 h2`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L01contra
msgid "You can use the §0 tactic in any proof to assume the\n"
"opposite of your goal.  But it is most useful when the goal\n"
"starts with the symbol §1.  After using the §2 tactic,\n"
"your goal will be §3.\n"
"\n"
"To complete a proof by contradiction, you must prove contradictory statements.\n"
"If your goal is §4 and you have assumptions §5 and §6, for\n"
"some statement §7, then §8 will close the goal.  Note that §9 won't\n"
"work; you must list the negative statement first to establish a contradiction."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `apply Subset.antisymm`
#. §1: `A ∩ B ⊆ B ∩ A`
#. §2: `B ∩ A ⊆ A ∩ B`
#. §3: `inter_subset_swap`
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L07inter_comm
msgid "As we saw in Complement World, a good first step when your goal is an equation between\n"
"sets is §0.  For the theorem in this level, that will leave you with\n"
"two goals: §1 and §2.  Fortunately, you can prove *both* of these\n"
"goals by using the theorem §3 from the last level."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `push_neg`
#. §1: `push_neg`
#. §2: `push_neg at h`
#. §3: `h`
#. §4: `apply`
#. §5: `push_neg`
#. §6: `apply`
#. §7: `compl_compl`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L04compcomp
msgid "The §0 tactic can reexpress a number of different kinds of negative statements as\n"
"equivalent positive statements; use\n"
"§1 to reexpress a negative goal, and §2 to reexpress a negative assumption §3.\n"
"We'll see many more uses of the §4 tactic in this game.\n"
"For more details about the use of these tactics,\n"
"click on §5 or §6 under the list of tactics on the right.\n"
"\n"
"We have given this theorem the name §7.  Both this theorem and the one in the previous\n"
"level will be useful in the next level."
msgstr ""

