#: Game.Levels.FamInter.L03interpair
msgid "If §0 denotes some object, then §1 denotes the set whose only element is §2; such a set\n"
"is called a *singleton* set.  Similarly, if §3 and §4 denote objects, then §5 denotes\n"
"the set whose elements are §6 and §7, and nothing else.  (Similar notation can be used to\n"
"denote a set containing any finite list of objects.  All of the objects in the list must\n"
"have the same type; if the objects have type §8, then the set has type §9.)\n"
"\n"
"There is another way to define sets.  If §10 is a statement about an\n"
"unspecified object §11, then §12 denotes the set of all values of §13 that make §14\n"
"come out true.  This is often called *set-builder notation*."
msgstr ""

