"is a theorem stating the definition.  If you have §0, §1, and §2,\n"
"then §3 is a proof of the statement §4.\n"
"That means you can use §5 to write out the definition of\n"
"§6 if it appears in any assumption or the goal.  (The similar theorem about intersections\n"
"was called §7.  Why isn't this one called §8?  I don't know.  The\n"
"naming of theorems in Lean is systematic, but there are occasional surprises.)"
