msgstr ""

#. §0: `h1 : A ⊆ B`
#. §1: `h2 : B ⊆ C`
#. §2: `h3 : x ∈ A`
#. §3: `h1 h3`
#. §4: `x ∈ B`
#. §5: `exact h1 h3`
#. §6: `h1 h3`
#. §7: `h4 : x ∈ B`
#. §8: `have`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L03have
msgid "In this level, we have assumptions §0, §1, and §2.\n"
"As we saw in the last level, §3 is a proof that §4.  Unfortunately,\n"
"that is not the goal, so we can't use §5 to close the goal.\n"
"However, we can use the proof §6 to justify adding §7 to our\n"
"list of assumptions.  To do that, we'll use a new tactic: §8."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A = B`
#. §1: `A`
#. §2: `B`
#. §3: `ext x`
#. §4: `x`
#. §5: `x ∈ A ↔ x ∈ B`
#: Game.Levels.Inter.L08inter_assoc
msgid "If your goal is §0, where §1 and §2 are sets, then the tactic §3 will introduce\n"
"a new arbitrary object §4 into the proof and set the goal to be §5."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h2}»`
#. §1: `obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := «{h2}»`
#. §2: `s`
#. §3: `hs : s ∈ F ∧ «{x}» ∈ s`
#. §4: `s`
#. §5: `«{h2}»`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion.L03unionsubunion
msgid "The assumption §0 is now an existential statement.  Thus, §1\n"
"will introduce a new object §2 and a new assumption §3 into the proof.\n"
"Once the witness §4 has been introduced, the assumption §5 becomes redundant, so it is\n"
"deleted."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `apply Subset.antisymm`
#. §1: `union_subset_swap`
#: Game.Levels.Union.L05union_comm
msgid "If you start your proof with §0, then you'll be able to use\n"
"the theorem §1 that you proved in the last level."
msgstr ""

